# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We are committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and inclusive environment for everyone. All contributors and participants are expected to communicate respectfully and help create a positive community.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

- Being respectful and considerate of others.
- Using welcoming and inclusive language.
- Accepting constructive feedback.
- Focusing on what is best for the community.
- Showing empathy toward other participants.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, offensive comments, and other conduct that creates an unsafe or uncomfortable environment.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of this Code of Conduct. They may take appropriate and fair action when unacceptable behavior occurs.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces and public spaces where an individual is representing the project or its community.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers. All reports will be reviewed and handled fairly and respectfully.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers will review reported incidents and may take actions such as a warning, removal of inappropriate content, temporary restrictions, or permanent removal from the project community, depending on the seriousness of the behavior.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is based on common open-source community standards and has been adapted for the Simple Interest Calculator project.
